[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Grob Opening"]
[Variation "Grob Opening: Grob Gambit Declined"]
[ECO "A00"]
[Character "gambit,solid"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "long-diagonal,e4-space"]
[Kind "gambit"]

1. g4 d5 { Takes the centre. White's g-pawn has loosened the king's side, and the real danger is the bishop on the long diagonal. }
2. Bg2 c6 { Covers b7 and d5, so the bishop on g2 has nothing to hit. The g4 pawn can wait. }
3. h3 ( 3. c4 dxc4 { Takes the pawn; with ...c6 played, Bxb7 would just lose the bishop. } ) ( 3. d3 Bxg4 { Wins a pawn: nothing defends g4 and the bishop is safe. } )
3... e5 { Takes space in the centre while White's king's side is loosened. }
4. d4 e4 { Shuts the g2 bishop in behind its own pawns. Plan: ...Nf6, ...Bd6 and castle queenside or kingside once White commits. } *
